   "gap": "Supply, inside the existence argument for thm:p15-conditional-existence, the written step showing that the Radon-Nikodym densities Z_+, Z_- obtained on (Omega, G, P|_G) satisfy int_A Z_pm dP = int_A Z_pm d(P|_G) = nu_pm(A) for every A in G and are P-integrable with E Z_pm = E X^pm (for example a proved lemma that integrals of nonnegative G-measurable functions against P|_G equal their integrals against P, via G-simple approximation and monotone convergence on both spaces, or thm:p15-expectation-law-integral applied to the identity map (Omega,F0)->(Omega,G)). As written, annex:p15.conditional-existence (handbook/annex/p15/conditional-expectation.tex lines 23-40) applies Radon-Nikodym on (Omega,G,P|_G) and then asserts P-integrability and the P-integrals int_A Z dP = nu_+(A) - nu_-(A) with no step or citation; no handbook result on the route states the P|_G-to-P integral identity, so the construction of a Z satisfying the P-integral identity and integrability required by def:p15-general-conditional-expectation has an unwritten step. All other elements of the component are present.",
